window.docContents[32].resolve({"/ProofObjects/#Logical-Foundations--ProofObjects___-The-Curry-Howard-Correspondence--Lean___s-Trusted-Computing-Base":{"contents":"\n\nThere is some overlap here and with the discussion of the TCB in Logic.lean.\nFor that matter, much of the discussion of logical connective proofs here\noverlaps with the presentation in Logic.lean. This split feels non-optimal\nto me. I wonder if we can consider some sort of merge of these two chapters.\n\n\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009ProofObjects: The Curry-Howard Correspondence","header":"10.8. Lean's Trusted Computing Base","id":"/ProofObjects/#Logical-Foundations--ProofObjects___-The-Curry-Howard-Correspondence--Lean___s-Trusted-Computing-Base"}});